r510 (F123) PREVIEW, approved for go-live. Frontend only. No SQL.
No SQL. No migration. styles.css untouched. Karratha copy untouched.

User Administration (User Management) gains a Role dropdown on the right of the
status tabs (All, Pending, Approved, Disabled, Rejected). It lists All roles
plus each distinct role in the loaded user list. Choosing one shows only those
users among the rows already on screen.

The All tab still hides Disabled accounts until Show disabled (N). A role that
exists only on those hidden accounts is still in the dropdown. The table is
empty until Show disabled or the Disabled tab, and the empty line says how
many of that role stay hidden.

Undo: revert this PR. Nothing to undo in the database.

Try it
  Sign in as an administrator. Open User Management (User Administration).
  The Role dropdown sits on the status-tab row, label "Role", first option
  "All roles". Pick Controller, Salesperson or Administrator. The table
  narrows with no refresh. All roles puts the full status list back.
  Pending, Approved, Disabled and Rejected keep working, and Show disabled
  still only affects the All tab.
